Useful stuff indeed, but if I get a wish early in the game, its always
for blessed +3 speed boots.  These are the single most powerful item
in the game (IMHO).  They essentially double the damage of your weapon
when you choose to fight, and give you the option of running away when
its prudent.  Typically, I'll pick up the gray dragon mail with the
w.o.w. from the castle.

Some good late game wishes (assume you've already got Mojo, speed boots,
gray dragon mail, etc): 

 a blessed spellbook of remove curse - handy spell for when a lich or the
  wiz curses your bag of holding.  Otherwise carry some holy water in a
  regular sack (or blessed scrolls of remove curse).

 a blessed spellbook of clairvoyance - you can get amulet-style clairvoyance
  even before you find the wiz.  Clairvoyance can also be purchased from
  a temple priest.

 3 blessed tins of black dragon meat - if you haven't felt "firm" yet,
  this gives you three shots at it.

 a blessed luckstone - always useful, and sometimes hard to find.


